From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Sun, 04 Oct 2026 15:37:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: allow two Polaris SLPI FastRPC sessions

The sensor listener keeps one FastRPC descriptor for coherent rpcmem
allocation and opens a separate descriptor for its sensor-PD transport.
The inherited SDM845 context bank defaults to a single session, so the
second open fails with EBUSY. Sensor initialization never completes and
the firmware watchdog eventually restarts SLPI.

Allow both connections to share Polaris's existing SID 0 context bank
using the existing qcom,nsessions binding. SSC clients use QRTR and do
not need additional FastRPC sessions.

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-polaris.dts
@@ -6,6 +6,11 @@
 	glink-edge {
 		fastrpc {
 			qcom,protection-domain = "tms/servreg", "msm/slpi/sensor_pd";
+
+			compute-cb@0 {
+				/* Separate coherent allocator and sensor RPC connections. */
+				qcom,nsessions = <2>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 };
